WEBVTT

NOTE
Journey: Advocates - Week 15 Leader Video
Unit 4, Lesson 3: Agency

1
00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:08.140
The ability to choose.

2
00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:14.740
In fact, so many questions about why things happen are answered with just simply

3
00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:17.820
humanity's ability to make a choice.

4
00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:23.380
And choices really are what governs so much of our lives from the easiest decisions

5
00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:28.980
to some of the hardest to choices that take forever to make

6
00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:31.420
and ones that we make in an instant.

7
00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:37.380
And it's choices that are so powerful, and they're a privilege, and

8
00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:41.400
they're a responsibility, and it's something that God has given us.

9
00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:46.920
And this is one of those, again, one of those pointers to who God is and the fact

10
00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:49.540
that he exists. But here's the key question.

11
00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:54.560
How do students' choices—how do all of our choices,

12
00:00:54.620 --> 00:01:00.320
actually—reflect God? How do the things that we choose, whether it be right,

13
00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:06.340
whether it be wrong, good, bad, ugly, whatever it is, how do those choices reflect

14
00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:09.300
God? Some of our choices obviously do.

15
00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:12.480
A lot of our choices obviously don't.

16
00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:16.940
But when we talk about our ability to choose and the fact that God gave it to us,

17
00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:20.780
there's some things we really have to make sure we nail down with our students.

18
00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:23.500
So we're challenging students with two things.

19
00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:28.700
Number one, that our free will points us to him.

20
00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:32.640
The fact that we have free will is a pointer to who he is.

21
00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:37.540
It helps us understand that because we have the ability to choose, that God is out

22
00:01:37.540 --> 00:01:42.680
there somewhere. But number two, our free will should reflect him.

23
00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:48.960
And how we behave as Christians ought to be a reflection of who he is.

24
00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:52.960
So as you go about your unit this week, I want you to keep something in mind.

25
00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:57.700
Last week we took a temperature of our students to figure out where the students

26
00:01:57.700 --> 00:02:01.940
are. This week I want you to take temperature of your community.

27
00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:06.240
Now we talked at the very beginning about the importance of establishing a

28
00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:10.380
community, a strong community, a community that is open, one that loves, one that's

29
00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:12.700
close, one that students feel safe in.

30
00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:16.880
We talked about that kind of being an overarching goal of being able to communicate

31
00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:20.780
truth and love is to have a community where students feel safe to ask questions and

32
00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:24.420
so forth. So how is that community doing, right?

33
00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:28.160
How is it working? Are there adjustments that you need to make?

34
00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:33.740
It's so easy, especially as a leader of large groups to figure out, okay, how are

35
00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:37.160
all these groups working? Is there other issues or they're not?

36
00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:39.860
Does everybody feel like they belong?

37
00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:44.340
Even if you only do a small group yourself, it's really easy to get caught up and

38
00:02:44.340 --> 00:02:49.040
forget about maybe one particular student that has a ton of really great things to

39
00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:53.220
say but for some reason doesn't feel like they can say those things.

40
00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:58.340
So it's good to take a step back, take a look at our communities and see are we

41
00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:00.420
hitting the mark about where we want to be?

42
00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:02.160
So a couple things I want you to think about.

43
00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:04.780
Are leaders providing the right atmosphere?

44
00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:10.600
Are they crafting that sort of atmosphere of discussion when the questions are

45
00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:15.540
welcome one of grace and love but with truth and not letting one student

46
00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:17.840
dominate, inviting all students to participate.

47
00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:23.080
All of those pieces of the puzzle is the right kind of atmosphere being fostered.

48
00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:29.220
Number two, are students being loved and are they being challenged?

49
00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:34.140
So often we kind of confuse the two and we think that if we're loving students and

50
00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:36.640
we're just kind of letting them think what they want to think and we're, you know,

51
00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:42.660
in my experience, the most challenged students that I had in

52
00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:48.120
terms of how much I challenged them were the ones that felt most loved at the

53
00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:53.300
end of a year. Those are the ones that, you know, felt like they were valued.

54
00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:59.700
Go to any school in any classroom where in the middle of things students

55
00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:05.620
are frustrated, they're under pressure, and they think a teacher

56
00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:08.960
or somebody is really too hard on them and they complain about it.

57
00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:14.900
If you notice, go back to those schools and ask those teachers how many graduates

58
00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:18.900
come back to see them and the number's probably pretty high

59
00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:25.780
the more so it sort of works this way the more challenging you are with a student

60
00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:32.260
the greater respect you gain and the greater love that you are showing them it

61
00:04:32.260 --> 00:04:36.140
just works that way so make sure that you love them but make sure you also challenge

62
00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:40.140
them Number three, do they feel safe to be honest?

63
00:04:41.060 --> 00:04:43.920
I mean if we're loving them properly then that's probably going to be the case that

64
00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:47.340
they do feel safe. But there are some things that you know we want students to be

65
00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:53.220
honest but sometimes their honesty causes us to have to react in a way that they

66
00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:56.160
don't want us to react. But do they feel safe?

67
00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:58.960
Do they feel like they can be honest with us and then we're gonna react

68
00:04:58.960 --> 00:04:59.560
appropriately?

69
00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:05.400
Number four, are your small groups serving one another.

70
00:05:05.980 --> 00:05:09.000
Are you guys in your small groups caring for one another?

71
00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:13.080
Have you created a community where you love each other, where the students are

72
00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:17.040
loving on each other? It isn't just a place where you kind of come together, say a

73
00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:20.980
few things, and then off you go into something else and off to your real friends or

74
00:05:20.980 --> 00:05:21.840
whatever the case is.

75
00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:28.080
Are your small groups becoming a tight-knit community of people who care and love

76
00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:32.840
for one another? Now I would encourage you as a next step for that is to take those

77
00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:36.640
and get those students out into the community, whether it be the wider community or

78
00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:40.680
even just the church community, and find places for them to serve together and do

79
00:05:40.680 --> 00:05:43.600
things together to help build and foster that kind of community.

80
00:05:43.980 --> 00:05:47.240
All right, so you've almost made it to the halfway point.

81
00:05:47.560 --> 00:05:51.700
Congratulations. Keep it up. You guys are doing a great job, I am sure.

82
00:05:51.920 --> 00:05:56.000
And remember, some of your students might be starting to feel some of the stress of

83
00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:59.780
school because you're probably getting around midterms and finals and tests and

84
00:05:59.780 --> 00:06:00.900
quizzes and those kinds of things.

85
00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:05.700
So now would be a really good time, and this is a really good lesson to do some fun

86
00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:10.480
things, to have some fun with students on making choices, whether it be through

87
00:06:10.480 --> 00:06:14.700
games, whether it be through examples, something silly, but you could have a whole

88
00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:19.620
bunch of fun having students make choices, but at the same time teach them the power

89
00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:20.240
of those choices.

